cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Spherical Sampling Exploration: Reconstruction Accuracy of Classical and Polyhedral Sampling Schemes on the Sphere"
abstract: >-
  A set of Jupyter notebooks exploring sampling schemes on the sphere and the
  accuracy with which a bandlimited spherical function can be reconstructed
  from samples taken on each one. Compares classical quadrature-based grids
  (Driscoll-Healy, Gauss-Legendre, McEwen-Wiaux) against polyhedral grids
  built by refining tetrahedral, octahedral and icosahedral meshes.
type: software
authors:
